    {
      "source": "Known since ancient times, the constellation Taurus is represented by just the front half of the bull. It includes two open star clusters (groups)—the Hyades and Pleiades. A bright red star, Aldebaran, marks one eye. Taurus is most easily seen during November and December. It is almost impossible to see in May and June because it is too close to the Sun.",
